Subject: [M152] Prevent UAF during re-entrant destruction in IME callouts.

Original change's description:
> Prevent UAF during re-entrant destruction in IME callouts.
>
> During IME callouts (such as SetVirtualKeyboardVisibilityIfEnabled or
> NotifySelectionBoundsChanged), the RenderWidgetHostViewAura or the
> updated view can be re-entrantly destroyed or unregistered. This CL adds
> weak pointer checks and re-fetches the text input state after these
> callouts to prevent accessing freed memory. A unit test is added to
> verify the fix when destruction occurs during virtual keyboard
> visibility updates.
>
